# Marketplace snapshot keys (claude-agents decision 0114 section 1; security review of stigready-web#74), OpenSSH allowed_signers format:
#   snapshot@stigready namespaces="stigready-marketplace-snapshot" ssh-ed25519 AAAA... <comment>
# The live/marketplace branch can be pushed by any repo writer, so copy-truth and copy-drift-watch trust
# marketplace-live.json only with marketplace-live.json.sig, made by stigready's marketplace-live-snapshot job with
# `ssh-keygen -Y sign -n stigready-marketplace-snapshot` and a private key only that job can read (Vault). Only
# ssh-ed25519 lines with exactly that principal and namespace, and no cert-authority, count.
#
# The checks read this file from their own tree (the base branch in pull request runs). A change to it is
# removal-class in copy-removal-gate. While no key is listed, copy-truth and copy-drift-watch exit 2 (production state
# unknown): both are advisory or unscheduled until then.
